'''20 Carrer Verd''' (formerly '''Torre CIEA''') is a 40-storey office tower at 20 Carrer Verd in the [[Districte Financer (Original, Sant Cristòfor)|Districte Financer]] of [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Sant Cristòfor]], [[Balboa]]. Completed in 1985, the building was originally constructed as the corporate headquarters of [[CIEA]], the largest energy company in Balboa, and was known as the Torre CIEA. It remains CIEA's current headquarters while the company's new tower, the [[Torre CIEA]] at 400 [[Avinguda Embarcadero]], is under construction. Upon completion of the new tower in 2028, the building will be renamed 20 Carrer Verd and converted to multi-tenant office use.

== History ==

The tower was completed in 1985 during the [[Balboa real-estate bubble|real-estate bubble]], when CIEA commissioned a purpose-built headquarters in the Districte Financer. At 170 metres, it was among the tallest buildings in Sant Cristòfor at the time of its completion and served as the company's principal corporate address for nearly four decades.

In the 2020s, CIEA announced plans for a new, larger headquarters — the [[Torre CIEA]] at 400 Avinguda Embarcadero, a 75-storey tower planned at 350 metres. Construction of the new tower began in 2023. The original building will continue to serve as CIEA's headquarters until the new tower's estimated completion in 2028, at which point it will be renamed 20 Carrer Verd — taking its address as its new designation — and converted from a single-tenant corporate headquarters to a multi-tenant office tower.

== Use ==

20 Carrer Verd currently serves as the headquarters of [[CIEA]]. Upon the completion of the [[Torre CIEA]] in 2028, the building will be converted to multi-tenant office use, with office floors leased to financial services firms, law offices, and professional services tenants, taking advantage of its location in the Districte Financer and its proximity to the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] and the waterfront.

